menu "Picters kernel extras"

config PICTERS_PERF
	bool "Picters in-kernel CPU frequency caps"
	depends on CPU_FREQ
	default n
	help
	  Exposes /sys/kernel/picters_perf, where a per-cpufreq-policy maximum
	  frequency can be pinned with a FREQ_QOS_MAX request. Unlike a write to
	  scaling_max_freq, the vendor perf HAL cannot raise it again, so a power
	  profile holds without a userspace re-apply loop. Caps are clamped into
	  each policy's own range, so nothing above stock can be requested.

	  If unsure, say N.

endmenu
